4.9 Cross‑Platform Abstraction

Purpose: Decouple the city’s intelligence from specific instruction set architectures, ensuring longevity.

Implementation:

· A hardware abstraction layer (HAL) translates the same high‑level control logic to:
  · ARM – wearables, sensor motes, drone flight controllers.
  · x86 – central servers, analytics clusters.
  · RISC‑V – open‑source science payloads, experimental quantum controllers.
  · Cloud – ground‑based simulation and backup instances.
· Containerisation via lightweight VMs allows seamless migration of services across ISAs during maintenance or hardware upgrades.

Benefit: When a new processor architecture emerges (e.g., RISC‑V vector extensions), the entire city software stack can be recompiled without redesign.

