7. Technical Feasibility and Challenges

Feasibility:

· Photonic AI and quantum annealing are already lab‑demonstrated; scaling to orbital deployment is an engineering challenge, not a physics impossibility.
· Compact fusion is under active development (e.g., SPARC, Helion); a space‑rated version may be viable by the 2040s.
· Real‑time Linux in space is proven (SpaceX Dragon, ISS laptops).

Challenges:

· Radiation hardening of photonic and quantum components.
· Thermal management in vacuum for dense compute clusters.
· Trust in autonomous ethical governance – requires unprecedented transparency and international oversight.
· Latency between Earth and orbit (400 ms round trip) – mandates that all critical intelligence be on‑board, not cloud‑dependent.
· Cost – a full‑scale Star Ring is a multi‑trillion dollar endeavour; the QUENNE stack is a fraction of that but still demands R&D investment.

